{"name":"Morris Room Grey","hex":"#ada193","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"morris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of pike.","A morris dance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform morris dancing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morris"},{"term":"room","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An opportunity or scope (to do something). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Space for something, or to carry out an activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reside, especially as a boarder or tenant.","To assign to a room; to allocate a room to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/room"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Room","blocks":[{"text":"In a building or a ship, a room is any enclosed space within a structure, typically bounded by walls to which entry is possible only via a door or other dividing structure. The entrance connects it to either a passageway, another room, or the outdoors. The space is typically large enough for several people to move about. The size, fixtures, furnishings, and sometimes placement of the room within the building or ship support the activity to be conducted in it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg/330px-Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Room","wikidata":"Q180516"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash